## 3. Dependency Injection and Inversion of Control

Components should not instantiate their own dependencies. Instead, dependencies are supplied from the outside (constructor injection, factory, or service locator). This decouples components from concrete implementations and enables testing with fakes.

**Implementation:** Accept dependencies through the constructor. Register components in a DI container or compose them manually at the application entry point.

```java
public class OrderService {
    private final PaymentGateway gateway;
    private final InventoryClient inventory;
    private final AuditLogger logger;

    public OrderService(PaymentGateway gateway,
                        InventoryClient inventory,
                        AuditLogger logger) {
        this.gateway = gateway;
        this.inventory = inventory;
        this.logger = logger;
    }

    public OrderResult placeOrder(Order order) {
        logger.log("Placing order " + order.getId());
        boolean paid = gateway.charge(order.getTotal());
        if (!paid) return OrderResult.rejected("Payment failed");
        inventory.reserve(order.getItems());
        return OrderResult.confirmed();
    }
}
```

**Example:** `OrderService` depends on three collaborators. In production, real implementations are injected; in tests, mocks replace them.

**Edge Cases:**
- A dependency is `null` (container misconfiguration).
- A dependency's method throws a runtime exception mid-flow.
- Circular dependencies between components.

**Tests:**
```java
@Test
void placeOrder_rejectsWhenPaymentFails() {
    PaymentGateway failingGateway = mock(PaymentGateway.class);
    when(failingGateway.charge(anyDouble())).thenReturn(false);
    OrderService service = new OrderService(failingGateway,
                                            mock(InventoryClient.class),
                                            mock(AuditLogger.class));
    OrderResult result = service.placeOrder(new Order("1", 99.99, List.of()));
    assertEquals(OrderResult.Status.REJECTED, result.getStatus());
}
```

